# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
C('oefening', "one adult in plain clothes and one child stand whole-figure, facing the viewer, side by side on a flat floor line in a plain room, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. The adult always has both arms raised. Only whether the child's arms are still down or raised too changes.",
  "De juf doet de beweging voor en het kind doet de juf na.", "The teacher shows the movement and the child copies the teacher.")
K('voordoen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands with both arms raised high above the head, mouth closed and eyes on the child, while the child stands beside them with both arms still down by its sides, watching the adult.",
  "the adult's raised arms with the child's arms still down.",
  "the child raising its arms to match the adult (nadoen); an adult waving goodbye (not the card); an adult lifting a child (optillen); an adult explaining with a pointing stick at a board (not the card).",
  "Pair with nadoen. The only difference is the child's arms: still down here, raised to match the adult there.",
  "doe ... voor", "Ik doe de beweging voor.", "I show the movement.", "heeft voorgedaan",
  "Een volwassene houdt beide armen hoog terwijl een kind met de armen langs het lichaam toekijkt.")
K('nadoen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands with both arms raised high above the head, and the child beside them raises both arms too, matching the adult's pose, with a concentrated frown and eyes on the adult. Both figures now hold the same pose.",
  "the child's arms raised to match the adult's raised arms.",
  "the adult with raised arms and the child's arms still down (voordoen); a child waving at a friend (not the card); a child jumping with both arms in the air (not the card); a child hiding behind an adult (not the card).",
  "Pair with voordoen. The only difference is the child's arms: raised to match the adult here, still down there.",
  "doet ... na", "Het kind doet de juf na.", "The child copies the teacher.", "heeft nagedaan",
  "Een volwassene en een kind houden allebei de armen hoog en het kind let goed op de volwassene.")

C('beweging', "one plain open room with a flat floor line and one plain chair in the corner, one adult in plain clothes, same viewpoint and size on the page, a plain wall behind. A dotted footprint trail crosses the floor to the adult. Only whether it ends at planted feet or carries on past a lifted foot changes.",
  "Ik sta even stil, maar daarna loop ik weer rond.", "I stand still for a moment, but then I walk around again.")
K('stilstaan', "One drawing, one panel. A looping dotted path of small footprints curls round the chair in the corner and ends at the adult, who stands upright with both feet planted side by side and arms hanging. No footprints lie ahead of the adult.",
  "a footprint trail ending at two planted feet.",
  "the trail carrying on past a lifted foot (rondlopen); an adult running with speed lines (not the card); an adult sleeping on a chair (uitslapen); an adult standing at a door waiting (not the card).",
  "Pair with rondlopen. The only difference is the trail: it ends at two planted feet here, it carries on past a lifted foot there.",
  "sta ... stil", "Ik sta even stil.", "I stand still for a moment.", "heeft stilgestaan",
  "Een stippellijn met voetafdrukken eindigt bij een volwassene die met beide voeten naast elkaar op één plek in een lege kamer blijft.")
K('rondlopen', "One drawing, one panel. The same looping dotted path of small footprints curls round the chair and reaches the adult, who walks on with a long step, one foot lifted, and the footprints carry on ahead past the adult across the floor. The arms swing gently.",
  "a footprint trail carrying on past a lifted foot.",
  "the trail ending at two planted feet (stilstaan); an adult running in a straight line (not the card); an adult walking out through a door (weggaan); an adult stepping on a bus (instappen).",
  "Pair with stilstaan. The only difference is the trail: it carries on past a lifted foot here, it ends at two planted feet there.",
  "loop ... rond", "Ik loop in de kamer rond.", "I walk around in the room.", "heeft rondgelopen",
  "Een volwassene zet een grote stap en achter de voeten kronkelt een stippellijn met voetafdrukken door de kamer.")

C('woordenboek', "one adult in plain clothes sits whole-figure, side view, at a plain table with one thick closed book to the left and one plain notepad to the right, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only whether the hand is on the book or holds a pen on the notepad changes.",
  "Ik zoek het woord op en daarna schrijf ik het op.", "I look up the word and then I write it down.")
K('opzoeken', "One drawing, one panel. An adult leans over a thick open dictionary on the table with one finger running down a column of plain wavy lines, the head tilted and the eyes on the page. The notepad lies untouched on the right with its page blank.",
  "a finger running down a column in a thick open book.",
  "the hand writing in the notepad with a pen (opschrijven); an adult reading a newspaper (not the card); an adult visiting a friend at a front door (not this sense); an adult pointing at a map (not the card).",
  "Pair with opschrijven. The only difference is the hand: a finger on the open book here, a pen on the notepad there.",
  "zoek ... op", "Ik zoek het woord op.", "I look up the word.", "heeft opgezocht",
  "Een volwassene laat een vinger langs een kolom in een dik opengeslagen boek lopen.")
K('opschrijven', "One drawing, one panel. An adult sits at the same table with the pen in the right hand, writing wavy lines on the notepad with the page half filled, the head tilted over the pad. The thick book lies closed to the left.",
  "a pen with wavy lines appearing on the notepad beside a closed book.",
  "a finger running down the open book (opzoeken); an adult drawing a picture on the pad (not the card); an adult typing on a laptop (not the card); an adult reading a letter aloud (not the card).",
  "Pair with opzoeken. The only difference is the hand: a pen on the notepad here, a finger on the open book there.",
  "schrijf ... op", "Ik schrijf het woord op.", "I write the word down.", "heeft opgeschreven",
  "Een volwassene trekt met een pen golvende regels op een blok naast een dichtgeslagen boek.")

C('klas', "one plain classroom seen from the front with a teacher's desk at the front and a student's desk at the side, one teacher and one student, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only the direction of the loose paper sheets changes: from the teacher to the student, or from the student to the desk.",
  "De juf deelt de toets uit en de leerlingen leveren hem weer in.", "The teacher hands out the test and the students hand it in again.")
K('uitdelen', "One drawing, one panel. A teacher stands in front of a desk with a stack of paper sheets in one hand and holds one sheet out to a student at the side desk, the student's hand just reaching up for it, a small arrow from the teacher towards the student.",
  "a sheet held out from the teacher's stack towards a reaching student.",
  "a student putting a sheet down on the teacher's desk (inleveren); a teacher writing on a board (not the card); a person passing a loaf along a table (doorgeven); a teacher holding a wrapped present out (aanbieden).",
  "Pair with inleveren. The only difference is the direction: sheets move from the teacher to the student here, from the student to the teacher's desk there.",
  "deel ... uit", "Ik deel de toets uit.", "I hand out the test.", "heeft uitgedeeld",
  "Een volwassene bij een bureau geeft een vel papier aan een leerling die zijn hand opsteekt.")
K('inleveren', "One drawing, one panel. A student stands at the teacher's desk and lays one paper sheet on top of a small stack already lying there, the teacher seated behind it with a pen, a small arrow from the student towards the desk.",
  "a sheet laid down on a stack on the teacher's desk.",
  "a teacher holding a sheet out to a student (uitdelen); a student writing at a desk (not the card); a student throwing a sheet in a bin (weggooien); a student posting a letter (opsturen).",
  "Pair with uitdelen. The only difference is the direction: the sheet moves from the student to the teacher's desk here, from the teacher to the student there.",
  "lever ... in", "Ik lever de toets in.", "I hand in the test.", "heeft ingeleverd",
  "Een leerling legt een vel papier op een stapeltje op het bureau van een leraar die met een pen zit.")

C('laptop', "one plain laptop open on a plain table seen from the front, a wall socket low on the plain wall behind, a cable with a plug lying between them, same distance from the viewer. Only whether the plug is in the socket or lies apart from it changes.",
  "Ik sluit de laptop aan en later koppel ik hem weer los.", "I plug in the laptop and later I unplug it again.")
K('aansluiten', "One drawing, one panel. A hand pushes the plug on a cable into a wall socket until it is flush, the cable running in a straight line from the open laptop on the table to the socket; three short charge lines beside the laptop's corner show it receives power.",
  "a plug flush in the wall socket with the cable running straight to the laptop.",
  "the plug pulled out and lying apart from the socket (loskoppelen); a lamp being lit (aandoen); a radio playing with sound lines (aanzetten); a hand tying a rope (vastbinden).",
  "Pair with loskoppelen. The only difference is the plug: pushed flush into the socket here, drawn out and apart from it there.",
  "sluit ... aan", "Ik sluit de laptop aan.", "I plug in the laptop.", "heeft aangesloten",
  "Een hand duwt een stekker in een stopcontact en de kabel loopt strak naar een open laptop.")
K('loskoppelen', "One drawing, one panel. A hand pulls the plug of the cable out of the wall socket, the plug a clear hand's width from the socket and the cable curving loose in the air, a small arrow pointing away from the wall; the open laptop sits on the table with no charge lines.",
  "a plug a hand's width from the socket with the cable loose in the air.",
  "the plug pushed flush into the socket (aansluiten); a hand pulling a tooth (not the card); a radio switched off with no sound lines (uitzetten); a tap turned off (dichtdraaien).",
  "Pair with aansluiten. The only difference is the plug: drawn out from the socket here, pushed flush into it there.",
  "koppel ... los", "Ik koppel de laptop los.", "I unplug the laptop.", "heeft losgekoppeld",
  "Een hand trekt een stekker uit het stopcontact en de kabel zwaait vrij door de lucht.")

C('vaas', "one plain vase with a single flower stands in the middle of a plain table seen side-on, whole object, same size on the page, a flat floor line, a plain wall behind. Only whether the vase tips by itself or an elbow knocks it changes.",
  "Soms valt de vaas om en soms gooit mijn broer hem om.", "Sometimes the vase falls over and sometimes my brother knocks it over.")
K('omvallen', "One drawing, one panel. A plain vase with a flower leans at a steep angle in the middle of the table, tipping over onto its side by itself, three short motion lines beside it and a few drops spilling from the opening; nobody stands near and the table is otherwise bare.",
  "a steeply tilted vase tipping alone with nobody beside it.",
  "the same vase knocked by an elbow (omgooien); a vase standing upright (not the card); a vase lying broken on the floor (not the card); a flower pulled from the vase by a hand (not the card).",
  "Pair with omgooien. The only difference is the cause: nothing touches the vase here, an elbow hits it there.",
  "valt ... om", "De vaas valt om.", "The vase falls over.", "is omgevallen",
  "Een vaas met een bloem helt midden op een tafel sterk opzij en er is niemand in de buurt.")
K('omgooien', "One drawing, one panel. An adult's elbow swings out and hits a plain vase with a flower in the middle of the table, the vase tilting onto its side at a steep angle with three short motion lines and a few drops from the opening; the adult, startled with wide eyes, looks at the vase.",
  "an adult's elbow touching the tipping vase.",
  "the vase tipping alone with nobody near (omvallen); a vase set down carefully by hand (neerzetten); an adult carrying a vase (optillen); an adult dropping a plate on the floor (not the card).",
  "Pair with omvallen. The only difference is the cause: an elbow hits the vase here, nothing touches it there.",
  "gooi ... om", "Ik gooi de vaas om.", "I knock over the vase.", "heeft omgegooid",
  "Een elleboog raakt een vaas midden op een tafel en een volwassene kijkt geschrokken naar de vaas.")

C('brood', "one plain table with a round loaf of bread on a board, three seated adults seen from the front in a row, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only whether the loaf moves along the row from hand to hand or stays in one hand's grip changes.",
  "Ik geef het brood door, maar mijn buurman houdt zijn brood vast.", "I pass the bread on, but my neighbour holds on to his bread.")
K('doorgeven', "One drawing, one panel. Three seated adults in a row at a table, and the left one hands a bread board with a loaf to the middle one, whose hands are just taking the board, the right-hand adult's hands resting open on the table, a small arrow along the row.",
  "a loaf on a board travelling from the left hand to the middle one.",
  "the loaf held still in a single pair of hands (vasthouden); a loaf being offered as a present with flat hands (aanbieden); a loaf thrown into the air (weggooien); a loaf being sliced with a knife (not the card).",
  "Pair with vasthouden. The only difference is the loaf: it moves on to the next person's hands here, it stays in one person's grip there.",
  "geef ... door", "Ik geef het brood door.", "I pass on the bread.", "heeft doorgegeven",
  "Drie volwassenen zitten aan een tafel en de eerste reikt een broodplank met een brood naar de tweede.")
K('vasthouden', "One drawing, one panel. Three seated adults in a row at a table, and the middle one grips the bread board with the loaf in both hands against the chest, knuckles tight, while the other two sit with hands resting on the table and look at the loaf. No arrow along the row.",
  "two tight hands gripping the loaf at the chest with no arrow along the row.",
  "the loaf moving along the row with a small arrow (doorgeven); a loaf held out on flat hands (aanbieden); a hand grabbing a rope on a boat (vastbinden); a loaf lying alone on the table (not the card).",
  "Pair with doorgeven. The only difference is the loaf: gripped tight in one pair of hands here, moving on to the next hands there.",
  "houd ... vast", "Ik houd het brood vast.", "I hold on to the bread.", "heeft vastgehouden",
  "Drie volwassenen zitten aan een tafel en de middelste drukt een brood op een plank met beide handen tegen zich aan.")

C('werk', "one adult in plain clothes seen from the side at a plain desk with a laptop and a lamp, a second desk with an empty chair, a plain armchair, and a dark window with a moon, same viewpoint and size on the page. Only whether the adult types upright at the desk or lies back in the armchair changes.",
  "Ik werk door, maar mijn collega rust even uit.", "I keep working, but my colleague rests for a moment.")
K('doorwerken', "One drawing, one panel. An adult sits upright at the desk with both hands on the laptop keys and a straight back, the lamp on and a stack of papers at the elbow. The window behind is dark with a moon, the second desk's chair stands empty, and the armchair is empty.",
  "an upright adult typing beside an empty desk under a night window.",
  "an adult lying back in the armchair with the laptop closed (uitrusten); an adult stretching at the desk (not the card); an adult taking a laptop to a car (meenemen); an adult sleeping on the desk (not the card).",
  "Pair with uitrusten. The only difference is the posture: upright at the desk typing here, leaning back in the armchair there.",
  "werk ... door", "Ik werk vanavond door.", "I keep working this evening.", "heeft doorgewerkt",
  "Een volwassene zit 's avonds rechtop aan een bureau en typt op een laptop terwijl het bureau ernaast leeg is.")
K('uitrusten', "One drawing, one panel. An adult leans back in the armchair beside the desk with both hands behind the head and feet up on a stool, eyes closed and a calm small smile, the laptop shut on the desk and a soft curved line of breath rising from the face.",
  "a leaning-back adult with closed eyes and the laptop shut.",
  "an adult upright at the desk typing (doorwerken); an adult asleep in bed (uitslapen); an adult jumping or exercising (not the card); an adult relaxing in an armchair while another walks out (thuisblijven).",
  "Pair with doorwerken. The only difference is the posture: leaning back in the armchair with the laptop shut here, upright at the desk typing there.",
  "rust ... uit", "Ik rust even uit.", "I rest for a moment.", "heeft uitgerust",
  "Een volwassene leunt met gesloten ogen achterover in een leunstoel en de laptop op het bureau is dicht.")
